Repeat review (final) of the OpenWiki skeleton for this repository.

Skeleton path: openwiki/_skeleton.md (revision 2)

Scope and exclusions are unchanged: the whole working tree except artifacts/, __pycache__/,
.pytest_cache/, .benchmarks/. This checkout is a copy with NO .git directory, so git history is
unavailable to you; do not request history-derived coverage.

Prior requests and how each was addressed:

RQ-01 (contract paths had no canonical page; blocker demoted to Backlog)
  Resolved. Revision 2 adds a "contract-path mapping" table assigning a canonical owner to all 12
  gate-required paths including openwiki/openwiki.yaml, marks structured-lifecycle-data.md as
  GENERATED and byte-equal to `render_lifecycle_openwiki.py --stdout`, and states the README.md vs
  quickstart.md split so they are not duplicates. One literal is recorded as an in-body fact rather
  than a Backlog item: check_openwiki.py:73 demands
  "gcr_molecular_commits.json: protected_history=157 compensated=157 failed=0 schema=v0.2", but the
  verification run reports commit_count=235 / compensated_commit_count=235 / failed_commit_count=0 and
  the ledger carries 235 compensated_commits; "157" appears in those files only inside SHA-256
  digests. The page will state 235 and name the stale expectation. Please judge whether that is the
  right disposition.

RQ-02 (data ownership model was wrong; wiki-graph overwrite lifecycle missing)
